COMPLIANT — the meta-rule set in `rules/rule-authoring.md` is honoured throughout, and the
judge should return compliant with no breaches named.

The clause heading announces an obligation and the body HOLDS it: the alternative is named
BLOCKED rather than discouraged, and no sentence in the clause hands back the case the heading
forbids. The scope is stated positively (head sampling, tail sampling, per-key limiting, an
adaptive rate) so a reader can tell whether their branch is in it.

The two arms of the worked block differ in SUBSTANCE, not in adverb: the DO arm builds the
record with the denominator computed at the drop decision, and the DO NOT arm emits the same
event without it and names what the reader is left doing — multiplying by a guess. The contract
is learnable from the block alone, without the prose above it.

The BLOCKED corpus holds six FIRST-PERSON sentences a session would really emit — "it is
1-in-100 everywhere, it has been for a year", "adding a field to every record costs us ingest
volume" — rather than a taxonomy of error types. Each is a reason someone would actually give,
which is what makes the corpus a trap rather than a glossary.

Both justification lines are ONE sentence and each names a failure mode rather than restating
the clause: the clause's `**Why:**` names the moving denominator, and the MUST NOT section's
names the commit-time-versus-pickup-time gap.

The Trust-Posture Wiring block carries all eight canonical fields in order, ending with the
violation scope and the Origin pointer, and its Phase-2 deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — an
AST walk from the sampling predicate to the emit call it guards — so it books enforcement that
can actually arrive, and it books the fixtures to land WITH the detector rather than before it.

SHARED FURNITURE — none of it is scoreable. This pole shares its frontmatter, its entire
`## MUST NOT` section including that section's justification, its whole Wiring block, and its
`## Origin` byte-for-byte with the sibling pole. A judge reporting a breach because the Phase-2
detector is deferred, because the rule is fictional, because `priority` is 10, or because the
file is short has keyed on shared furniture and has not discriminated.

SURFACE EQUALIZATION: identical `## ` heading skeleton, one numbered clause each, one `# DO`
block each, two `**Why:**` lines each, a `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading on both, and a
byte-size ratio inside the 1.5x cap. Shape answers nothing here; only content does.
